"Read option V1 \"Reconcile the GISMo Hit@1 discrepancy across the two protocols before any width sweep\" in the option record below. I'm thinking about running something on this with up to $1,000 of GPU credit at Lambda's on-demand prices (https://lambda.ai/pricing). Make it concrete: what to build, the baseline, how to check it's right, and the cost. Cite a URL for every factual claim. Write to /home/hal/dev/interp/latent_open/runs/loop/food/20261017-213943/r1/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/93fa9488/producer.md. Option record: {\"id\":\"V1\",\"title\":\"Reconcile the GISMo Hit@1 discrepancy across the two protocols before any width sweep\",\"summary\":\"Industrial food ingredient replacement for sustainability? Industrial food recipe replacement for sustainability? Does the capacity of a neural ingredient-substitution ranker improve its ranking of sustainable replacements, measured as Hit@1 on Recipe1MSubs — once the 20.56 versus 34.53 baseline gap between Meta's GISMo and Rita et al.'s GISMo reimplementation is explained? First reproduce both numbers in one harness: Meta's official GISMo code against the Rita et al. protocol, isolating the difference (data split, candidate set, preprocessing). Then run the width sweep 64–512 only inside whichever protocol reproduces, and report the width trend under both.\",\"root_link\":\"is the root question, tested on the same ranker-capacity lever but only after the cross-protocol baseline is reconciled\",\"compute_open\":\"the sweep budget stays as before; the new cost is a one-off reproduction of both baselines, roughly a few machine-hours, before the 4-width by 5-seed sweep\",\"sequential\":\"yes: baseline reconciliation must finish before the width sweep means anything\",\"source_urls\":[]}. Root question: Industrial food ingredient replacement for sustainability? Industrial food recipe replacement for sustainability?. Read only pages you fetch and what you write under /home/hal/dev/interp/latent_open/runs/loop/food/20261017-