 you will tell a real difference from run-to-run noise. predictions.expected is the outcome you expect, if_lever, if_not or unsure, with one sentence why. scored_against says what the measured outcome is compared with to decide it is correct. Each source carries the exact sentence from the page that you rely on. In restructuring, sequential_part is the part of this computation that one answer waits on step after step, and how many steps; method is why those steps need not run in order and how your plan computes them at the same time instead, or \"none\" if the plan only runs independent work side by side or splits each step across GPUs. If method is not none, also give condition, what must be true of this system for the method to pay off and the cheap measurement that checks it; condition_phase, the id of the phase that makes that measurement before the main spend; baseline_sequential, the fastest sequential implementation you will time and how it is tuned; and baseline_copies, independent copies run side by side on the same GPUs, which you will also time. Then compute_axis is the length of the chain or the number of runs the answer needs; predictions.if_lever and predictions.if_not say where on that axis, as numbers, the parallel version does or does not reach the same answer sooner than each baseline, and if_not says how you expect it to fail if it does; anchor checks the parallel result against the sequential one within a stated tolerance; test_summary names both baselines; and novelty.closest_prior is the nearest published parallel version of this computation. Write the record's card fields (question, hypothesis, predictions.if_lever, predictions.if_not, test_summary, novelty.closest_prior, novelty.left_open, anchor.what, limits, restructuring.sequential_part, restructuring.method) for a reader who has not seen your files: plain words, at most 25 words each (hypothesis and predictions.if_lever 22, anchor.what 24, novelty.closest_prior, novelty.left_open and limits 30, test_summary 45, restructuring.sequential_part 18, restructuring.method 22), no labels from your files or from the branch and framer files (write what C2 or E2 stands for, not the label), and keep every number the decision depends on. You may cite a source in any card field as [source id]. novelty.closest_prior is the published result that comes nearest to deciding between if_lever and if_not: what it measured and the largest amount of the compute quantity it used. novelty.prior_max_level is that amount in compute_axis.unit, or null if it is not on the same axis. novelty.decides says whether closest_prior already decides the outcome at your compute levels: no, partly or yes. novelty.searched says whether web search returned results while you planned. Run every local command under timeout. Start no new local run 45 minutes after you begin; if a run you need is unfinished by then, give its inputs basis GUESS with measured_by naming the phase that measures it. Local runs share a 4-core machine with other producers. Lambda's prices as read at the start of this run: {\"read_at\":\"2026-10-17\",\"instances\":[{\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA B200 SXM6\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":180,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":6.69,\"page_text\":\"NVIDIA B200 SXM6180 GB2082900 GiB22 TiB SSD$6.69\"},{\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA H100 SXM\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":80,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":3.99,\"page_text\":\"NVIDIA H100 SXM80 GB2081800 GiB22 TiB SSD$3.99\"},{\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":80,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":2.79,\"page_text\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM80 GB2401800 GiB19.5 TiB SSD$2.79\"},{\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":40,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":1.99,\"page_text\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM40 GB1241800 GiB5.8 TiB SSD$1.99\"},{\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA Tesla V100\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":16,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":0.79,\"page_text\":\"NVIDIA Tesla V10016 GB88448 GiB5.8 TiB SSD$0.79\"},{\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA B200 SXM6\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":180,\"n_gpus\":4,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":6.79,\"page_text\":